{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZaZCaVx78wNWHYmjzfM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment entity: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:1-34`\n- ShipmentController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:1-57`\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:1-28`\n- Error handling: ApiExceptions.kt (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException) and GlobalExceptionHandler.kt\n- ErrorCode enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- Tests: `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt:1-85`\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses (ConflictException for 409, ResourceNotFoundException for 404)\n2. GlobalExceptionHandler centrally converts exceptions to ApiError envelope\n3. ErrorCode enum contains machine-readable codes for all error cases\n4. Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions\n5. Tests have helper methods for creating test data\n6. Repository methods handle save, findById, existsById, findAll\n7. Status transitions are permanent (Shipment is immutable data class)\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — add confirm endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` — add SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code for cancelled rejection\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add tests for confirm scenarios\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding a new ErrorCode enum value could impact clients, but this is expected API evolution\n- Must ensure idempotency: confirming an already-confirmed shipment must succeed without error\n- State transition must only occur from CREATED to CONFIRMED, not from other states\n\n**Open questions:** None—the ticket is clear on all requirements.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the ErrorCode enum to represent the state conflict when attempting to confirm a cancelled shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add new endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment; throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new tests:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED status` — verify state transition\n   - `confirm is idempotent for CONFIRMED shipment` — retry without failure\n   - `rejects confirm with 409 for CANCELLED shipment` — verify error code\n   - `rejects confirm with 404 for unknown shipment` — verify ResourceNotFoundException\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- *Create a separate service class with business logic:* The existing codebase puts logic directly in the controller, and existing endpoints (create, getById) do the same. Adding a service layer would violate the principle of minimal change and introduce an unrelated refactoring.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Caller Receives | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|-----------------|-----------|\n| Confirm CREATED | shipment from repo | updated CREATED→CONFIRMED | 200 + Shipment | save() returns saved |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED (idempotent) | shipment from repo | nothing (no-op) | 200 + Shipment (unchanged) | findById only, no save |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | shipment from repo | nothing | 409 + error body | ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS |\n| Unknown ID | nothing | nothing | 404 + error body | ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. **Confirm CREATED shipment** — Create shipment, confirm it, assert status changed to CONFIRMED\n2. **Idempotent confirm** — Create shipment, confirm twice, second call should succeed with same response\n3. **Reject CANCELLED** — Set up cancelled shipment directly in repository, confirm should fail with 409/SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n4. **Reject unknown** — Attempt to confirm non-existent shipment, should fail with 404/SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":516,"cache_read_input_tokens":18358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":516},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d1cc8d0-31ab-4787-8b70-a0c3fb9913e4","uuid":"5502c852-0518-4f69-aa5b-8cdc62a1dc81","timestamp":"2026-09-30T11:54:46.169Z","request_id":"req_011CfZaZC8heH3YeBmxtTNsq"}
